## Right to Erasure: Requirements and Exceptions

### Requirements

The controller must erase personal data without undue delay where one of the following grounds applies (GDPR, Article 17(1)):

(a) The personal data are no longer necessary in relation to the purposes for which they were collected or otherwise processed;

(b) The data subject withdraws consent on which the processing is based, and there is no other legal ground for the processing;

(c) The data subject objects to the processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds, or objects to direct marketing;

(d) The personal data have been unlawfully processed;

(e) The personal data must be erased for compliance with a legal obligation in Union or Member State law;

(f) The personal data were collected in relation to the offer of information society services to children.

**Additional obligation:** Where the controller has made personal data public, the controller must take reasonable steps, including technical measures, to inform other controllers processing that data that the data subject has requested erasure of any links to, copies, or replications of those personal data (GDPR, Article 17(2)).

### Exceptions

The right to erasure does not apply to the extent that processing is necessary (GDPR, Article 17(3)):

(a) For exercising the right of freedom of expression and information;

